 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Family",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two independent MOSFET gate drivers per chip, each taking a TTL or CMOS logic level and driving a gate between GND and VDD. MAX626: both drivers inverting. MAX627: both non-inverting. MAX628: driver A inverting, driver B non-inverting. The MAX626 is pin-compatible with the TSC426 and the DS0026/DS0056, and the MAX626/7/8 are an improved second source for the TSC426/7/8. Delay changes little with VDD."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Switching power supplies, DC-DC converters, motor controllers, PIN diode drivers and charge-pump voltage inverters."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Inputs",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "An input must not dwell between VIL and VIH for more than 50 ns. An unused input goes to ground, which keeps the supply current low."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Parallel drivers",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "On the MAX626 and the MAX627 the two drivers can work as one: tie INA to INB and OUTA to OUTB."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Bypassing and ground",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Supply and output peak currents can exceed 2 A. On the inverting stages (MAX626, MAX628) ground drops act as negative feedback and slow the delay and transition times. Large dV/dt or large AC currents can cause ringing. Bypassing: 4.7 µF low-ESR in parallel with 0.1 µF ceramic, placed as close to the chip as possible. A ground plane, or separate input and output ground returns. A 5 Ω to 20 Ω series output resistor reduces ringing and may slow the output transitions."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power dissipation",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Dissipation has three parts: the input inverters, crowbar current through the output transistors during a transition, and the output current into a capacitive or resistive load. The three together are held within the package rating. The input inverters draw 0.4 mA DC with both inputs low and 4 mA with both inputs high. Crowbar current is about 100 mA for a few nanoseconds at each transition; it matters only at high switching frequency or with a light capacitive load (100 pF), and is otherwise a small share of the supply current."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply power",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Power consumption is 7 mW with the inputs low and 150 mW with the inputs high."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Die",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The die measures 0.076 in × 0.076 in (1.93 mm × 1.93 mm). INA and the driver A output pad are on one edge, INB and the driver B output pad on the opposite edge, GND and VDD on the other two edges. The output pads are /OUTA and OUTB on the MAX628, OUTA and OUTB on the MAX627, /OUTA and /OUTB on the MAX626."
  }
 ]
